      "content": "For adults and children 12 years and older, the recommended dose of Benadryl for an allergic reaction is 25-50mg. Taking two 50mg pills in a row might not be the best approach, as it can increase the risk of side effects like drowsiness and dry mouth. I would recommend taking one 50mg pill to start, and if symptoms persist or worsen, you can take another 50mg after 4-6 hours. If you're still concerned, consider contacting a healthcare provider or pharmacist for guidance on safe dosing timing.",
